# NOTE: this file is a Cloudflare Pages / Netlify convention. `emvycheck.com`
# is hosted on GitHub Pages (with Cloudflare only proxying DNS/CDN in front
# of it), and GitHub Pages does NOT read or execute a `_headers` file —
# confirmed live via `curl -I https://emvycheck.com/`, which showed none of
# the headers below (see docs/CC-09-09-LAUNCH-CLOSEOUT-v0.1.md's findings).
#
# Production enforcement of these headers is done at Cloudflare instead,
# via ONE Response Header Transform Rule scoped to emvycheck.com (Rules >
# Transform Rules > Modify Response Header in the Cloudflare dashboard).
# This file is kept as the documented source of the intended header
# policy — the values below are what the Cloudflare rule should match —
# but do not assume this file itself has any effect on what a visitor's
# browser actually receives. If GitHub Pages is ever replaced by a host
# that does read `_headers` (e.g. Cloudflare Pages), this file would take
# over automatically and the Cloudflare Transform Rule should be reviewed
# for redundancy at that point.
#
# 09/09 LAUNCH HARDENING v0.1: added ordinary browser-hardening headers
# below the original PHUL license block. No broad resource CSP — the site
# has inline CSS/JS and external media/forms that a strict CSP could break;
# only framing is restricted here.
#
# HSTS note: max-age is set WITHOUT includeSubDomains. cloud.emvycheck.com
# and staging.emvycheck.com are referenced in living-art-cloud/README.md
# but do not currently resolve in DNS; media.emvycheck.com and
# www.emvycheck.com do resolve and were confirmed HTTPS-safe. Since not
# every subdomain that might ever exist could be conclusively verified,
# the safer value (no includeSubDomains) was used for launch.

